\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Registration pipeline. The follow-up (moving) and baseline (fixed) PET/CT scans are aligned by an affine pre-registration, then by the LapIRN network, which predicts a dense deformation. Instance optimisation (IO) refines this deformation per pair before the moving scan is resampled into the fixed frame. Network training and IO use the same groups of loss terms: alignment, PET preservation, and deformation regularisation (Sec.\nobreakspace {}\ref {sect:objective}). \leavevmode {\color {red}[TODO: Update the figure if the rigidity term or the IO-only variant should appear.]}}}{4}{figure.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Losses in training and IO versus only in IO (test set, 28 patients). For each loss set, filled: network trained with the losses, then IO with them; hollow: network trained without them (T1), same IO. Grey: neither loss (I1). Points: patient means with 95\,\% patient-bootstrap confidence intervals.}}{18}{figure.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Per-lesion volume change on the test set (1327 lesions of 26 patients), by location (soft tissue / bone-associated, $\geq $50\,\% of the lesion on bone) and size (small $<$0.5\,ml, medium $<$5\,ml, large). Median $|\Delta \mathrm {MTV}|$ per lesion; left: network output, right: with instance optimisation (IO) using the same losses. Error bars: 95\,\% confidence intervals from a patient-cluster bootstrap. Lesions below 5 voxels are excluded.}}{19}{figure.3}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Patient-level results on the test set (28 patients; a patient's pairs are averaged). Violins: kernel density over patients, line: median; each dot is one patient. In brackets: where the PET and rigidity losses (PET + rig.) act; basic: IO with the similarity and regularisation terms only; both: training and IO. Initial alignment is omitted (CT Dice 9.5\,\%, HD95 44.4\,mm; MTV/TLG change 0 by construction, Table\nobreakspace {}\ref {tab:baselines}).}}{22}{figure.4}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Test pair with a large change in tumour volume (patient 0146; lesion volume 2400 voxels at baseline, 24191 at follow-up), registered by our network (PET and rigidity losses in training, no IO); one coronal slice. (a)\nobreakspace {}Fixed and (b)\nobreakspace {}moving CT with PET (SUV 0--8, 35\,\% opacity) and ground-truth lesion contours (red). (c,\nobreakspace {}d)\nobreakspace {}CT of the fixed scan (green) overlaid with the moving scan (magenta) before\nobreakspace {}(c) and after\nobreakspace {}(d) registration; grey where they agree. (e,\nobreakspace {}f)\nobreakspace {}Organ labels that differ before\nobreakspace {}(e) and after\nobreakspace {}(f) registration: green where the fixed scan has a label that the moving scan lacks there, magenta where only the moving scan is labelled; bright, medium, and dark shades for bones, organs, and muscles. (g)\nobreakspace {}Jacobian determinant of the transformation. (h)\nobreakspace {}Warped moving CT with PET and warped lesion contours.}}{23}{figure.5}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Effect of the PET loss weight in IO (test set): network trained without PET losses (T1) followed by IO with all PET weights scaled by the given factor (0: PET losses off; 1: the PET weights of network training). Each metric on the predicted labels that IO optimises (orange; organs: TotalSegmentator, lesions: nnU-Net) and on the ground-truth labels used for evaluation (blue). Dice over all 28 patients, lesion volume and uptake change over the 26 patients with lesions in both label sets. Solid: after IO; dashed: network output before IO, the same for every factor. Outlined point and dotted line: operating point tuned on the validation set. Points: patient means; bands: 95\,\% patient-bootstrap confidence intervals.}}{24}{figure.6}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Lesion volume and uptake change of ground-truth lesions, grouped by how much of each lesion the predicted lesion mask seen by IO covers: missed (214 lesions, 6\,\% of volume), partly covered (155 lesions, 6\,\% of volume), covered (1066 lesions, 88\,\% of volume). Test set; network trained without PET losses, IO with the PET weights scaled by the given factor. Left: change within each group (per scan, the change of the summed volume or uptake of the group's lesions; mean over the patients with lesions in the group). Right: contribution of each group to the evaluation metric (the change per scan if only the group's lesions changed; mean over patients); black: the evaluation metric, below the stacked total because changes of different lesions in a scan partly cancel.}}{25}{figure.7}%
